{
  "comment": "Generated by ir (cd ir && go test -run TestWriteMemoryStoreParityVectors -update); do not edit. The Go, TypeScript and Rust memory store runtimes each run every case of every section (D75). names: {name, declaration, parts, store?, member?, want, fullName?}. Build the name of declaration with parts, each part already in its wire string, as memorystore.Name does: the declaration, then ':' and each part. Every segment, the declaration and each part, is 1 to 128 bytes of UTF-8 with no ':', '*', '?', '[', ']', '@', '\\', byte below 0x20 or 0x7f, and is refused, never escaped. want is the name without the store's prefix, or null when it is refused; the reason is not compared. With store set, fullName is the name the store keys or publishes under: the prefix, which is store, or store@member when member is set, then ':' and the name; a store or a member that is no segment is refused, want and fullName null. rateLimit.windows: {name, limit, windowMs, nowMs, prevCount, currCount, want}. The shared rate limit's sliding window: curr = floor(nowMs / windowMs) * windowMs, prev = curr - windowMs, elapsed = nowMs - curr; estimate = prevCount * (windowMs - elapsed) / windowMs + currCount in IEEE doubles, in that order; this is the rule of the Go runtime's limiter, httprate: the request is allowed when round(estimate) + 1 <= limit, rounding half away from zero, and then increments the counter of the window starting at curr with a TTL of 2 * windowMs + 5000 ms; otherwise it is refused with Retry-After the window's length in whole seconds, windowMs / 1000. want: {allowed, estimate, currWindowStart, prevWindowStart (Unix seconds), incrementTtlMs (0 when refused), retryAfterSeconds (0 when allowed)}. rateLimit.keys: {name, service, operation, windowStart, clientKey, want}: the name, without the store's prefix, of the reserved rate-limit declaration's counter: rate-limit:<service>:<operation>:<windowStart in Unix seconds, base 10>:<lowercase hex SHA-256 of the UTF-8 clientKey>, or null when service or operation is no segment. Every server names the operation <namespace>.<name>, the namespace its generated operation table holds (the operation set's name in kebab case, less its Queries, Mutations, Operations or Actions suffix, root for Query and Mutation) and the operation's name: product.getProduct for ProductQueries.getProduct.",
